  "body": "## What changed\n\nPast a 90-degree head tilt, the tool axis of a 3+2 plane points down toward the machine table. The move from the tool-change height along that axis to the clearance plane can end under the table top. Before this PR, #2987 gave only a note in that case, and the post did not stop.\n\n- `crates/sim/src/verify/types.rs`: new `Warning::FirstTraverseUnderTable { at, height_mm, limit_mm }`. The text says \"lower the clearance plane to Z<limit> or under it\". It never says \"raise\". The verdict blocks the post (`blocks_post` is true).\n- `crates/app/src/operation/first_traverse.rs`: `TableRead::Unjudged` is now `Under { limit }`, with `limit = low + stroke / -axis_z` (`low` is the lowest start reading along the axis). `judge` pushes this verdict beside the stock and fixture verdict. The note is removed.\n- `crates/app/src/operation/stamp.rs`: the salt `first-traverse-table-3081` is added for each operation with a tilt. A tilted cache that the old law judged reads Stale one time. Without the salt, an old cache keeps the note, has no verdict, and posts.\n- Exhaustive matches: `warned_moves.rs`, `mcp/job.rs` (kind `first_traverse_under_table`), and `crates/ui/src/operations.rs` (fold key 224 and `last_move`). Key 222 is used by open PR #2836 and key 223 by open PR #3062, so this PR uses 224.\n- Examples: the tilted operations of `examples/catalog/multiaxis/indexed/indexed.camproj`, `examples/first-4axis-part.camproj` and `examples/guide-multiaxis.camproj` are restamped. Only the stamps change. Regenerated by the new law, the warnings, notes and moves are the same (max deviation 5e-7 mm, the rounding of the file). No `.nc` file changes.\n- Decision: `docs/decisions/3081-table-down-axis-verdict.md`. It uses the premise of #2987: the unknown start is at the tool-change height (the Z travel top). The law does not cover a program that starts with the tool low near the table.\n\n## Readings\n\nB 120 on the test machine (X +-400, Z stroke 300): the limit is 113.590 along the axis. A plane at 150 is refused. Planes at 100 and 113 pass.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `first_traverse_table::a_head_tilt_past_90_under_the_table_is_refused_with_lower` (replaces `a_head_tilt_past_90_names_the_table_unjudged`)\n- `first_traverse_table::a_head_tilt_past_90_plane_under_the_limit_passes`\n\n## Quick gate (head e82ca1d2d, -j 18)\n\n- Green: app `first_traverse_table`, `first_traverse`, `first_traverse_rotary`, `tilt_basis_compat`, `stale_rapid_law`, `machine_switch`, `example_catalog`, `continuous_4axis_part`, `setup_align_multiaxis` and `first_4axis_part`.\n- Green: `camcraft-ui` lib tests.\n- Clean: `cargo clippy -p camcraft-sim -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`.\n- Heavy lanes: not run, covered by the cut gate.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- In the refused test rig, the B 120 face also goes past the Z stroke, so the machine limit law refuses the post first. The test asserts these items:\n  - the cached verdict;\n  - `blocks_post`;\n  - the verdict text;\n  - that the post is refused.\n- The test does not assert the post error text for this verdict alone. `posting.rs` sends each cached warning for which `blocks_post` is true to the post gate.\n- An existing fold-key collision is not changed here: `AvoidHit` (part false) and `DrillUndersize` both use key 216. Open PR #3062 corrects it.\n\nChangelog: A 3+2 plane whose tool axis points down toward the table (head tilt past 90 degrees) is now refused when the first move from the tool-change height can go under the table top, with the plane height to lower to.\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #3081\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
